{"script": "export const meta = {
  name: 'ai-table-ui-check',
  description: 'Wait for one AI-table UI ticket run in its Sol-high Codex thread, then refute it with Sonnet (reusable: args id, threadId, runId, round, extra)',
  phases: [{ title: 'Check', detail: 'Haiku low waits for the Codex run; Sonnet medium refutes the pushed head' }],
}
const HUB = 'claude-code-game-master'
const T = `${HUB}/build/ai-table-ui-tickets`
const a = args
phase('Check')
const rep = await agent(`Your only job: wait for a T3 thread run to finish and return the thread's final reply verbatim. Do not send messages, do not do other work.
1) Call the t3-code tool t3_thread_wait with threadId ${JSON.stringify(a.threadId)}${a.runId ? `, runId ${JSON.stringify(a.runId)}` : ''} and timeoutMs 1800000. If it returns timedOut=true, call it again; repeat up to 20 times.
2) When it returns, call t3_thread_read with that threadId, view "messages", maxCharsPerItem 20000, paging with afterPosition (nextPosition) until hasMore is false; take the LAST assistant message${a.runId ? ' of that run' : ''}.
3) Answer: first line "STATUS: <terminal status>", then that last assistant message verbatim. If the tools fail, answer "WAIT_FAIL: <reason>".`, { label: `wait:${a.id}`, phase: 'Check', model: 'haiku', effort: 'low' })
if (/^\s*WAIT_FAIL/.test(rep || '')) return { rep, ref: null }
const ref = await agent(`You are the refuter of AI-table UI ticket ${a.id} (round ${a.round}). Read ${T}/COMMON.md and ${T}/${a.id}.md (if it exists) for the context, rules and the DoD — the same rules bind you, except that you do NOT edit the branch.
The implementer's report is below. Try to break it on the pushed head of v52-ui (\`ssh orchestra-vps\`, worktree /home/kesha/projects/ai-table-mvp-ui). First confirm the head moved since the previous round if this is a fix round. Use the implementer's fresh rig log if it is for the current head, else run one yourself through the heavy lock (a lone red test_i6_audio_barrier: rerun it alone 3 times and judge it as the known flake). Re-run the claimed mutants and add 5+ of your own on the new code in a /tmp clone (keep your mutation log in /home/kesha/ai-table-evidence/${a.id}/refute${a.round}.log); check no frozen check was weakened (diff the frozen files vs main 42f6921 and the I1 hashes); check that no function or data-testid of the old UI was silently lost (BRIEF §5 inventory); check the UI oracles ENFORCE on the redesigned surfaces; look at the screenshots against the concept slide and the design skill's hard rules (one primary action, word budgets, both long sides, no scroll, no emoji). ${a.extra || ''}
Write your report to ${T}/${a.id}-refute${a.round}.md and also answer with it. Its FIRST line is exactly "VERDICT: PASS" or "VERDICT: FAIL"; then defects with file:line, repro and fix direction, ≤ 100 lines. Keep a progress note in /home/kesha/ai-table-evidence/${a.id}/refute${a.round}-progress.md in case the hub restarts (read it first if it exists).
IMPLEMENTER REPORT:\n${rep}`, { label: `refute${a.round}:${a.id}`, phase: 'Check', model: 'sonnet', effort: 'medium' })
return { rep, ref }
", "args": {"id": "V-53", "threadId": "mcp:264d8ebd-3c43-41ad-82d9-32ee58bfa4a3", "runId": "run:thread:mcp%3A264d8ebd-3c43-41ad-82d9-32ee58bfa4a3:ordinal:4", "round": 3, "extra": "Round 3 = after the fix round. Recheck exactly D1, D3, D5, D6, D7, D8 from V-53-refute1.md/refute2.md and anything the fix touched. D2 and D4 (V-52 residual survivors) are deliberately NOT fixed: they wait for the owner's decision; only check that a TODO.md entry lists them, and do not fail the verdict on them."}}

